✅ 1. Definition
| Feature     | **Spring**                                     | **Spring Boot**                                                          |
| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| What is it? | A **framework** for building Java applications | A **framework built on top of Spring** to simplify setup and development |
| Use Case    | Gives flexibility but requires more setup      | Rapid development with less configuration                                |


✅ 2. Setup and Configuration
| Feature       | **Spring**                                 | **Spring Boot**                                       |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| Configuration | Manual XML or Java-based configuration     | **Auto-configuration** using `@SpringBootApplication` |
| Web Server    | Needs to be set up manually (e.g., Tomcat) | Comes with **embedded servers** (Tomcat, Jetty)       |


✅ 3. Project Structure
| Feature          | **Spring**                                    | **Spring Boot**                           |
| ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Boilerplate Code | Requires more code and structure upfront      | Minimal boilerplate with defaults         |
| Dependencies     | Need to define versions manually in `pom.xml` | Uses **Spring Boot Starter** dependencies |


✅ 4. Development Speed
| Feature | **Spring**            | **Spring Boot**                               |
| ------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Speed   | Slower to get started | Much faster to start and develop applications |


✅ 5. Key Annotations
| Purpose              | **Spring**                       | **Spring Boot**                        |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Main Entry           | Not defined                      | `@SpringBootApplication` (entry point) |
| REST API             | `@Controller`, `@RequestMapping` | Same, but works out-of-the-box  | //It means that in Spring Boot, you don’t have to configure anything manually for those annotations to function.
| Dependency Injection | `@Autowired`                     | Same                                   |


✅ 6. Build Tools
| Feature | **Spring**     | **Spring Boot**                                     |
| ------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Tools   | Maven / Gradle | Maven / Gradle (with **Spring Initializr** support) |


✅ 7. Use Cases
| Use Case              | **Spring**                        | **Spring Boot**                               |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Large enterprise apps | Yes (when full control is needed) | Yes (but better for microservices, REST APIs) |
| Quick prototyping     | Less suitable                     | Perfect for quick development                 |


🎯 Summary
| Feature        | Spring   | Spring Boot |
| -------------- | -------- | ----------- |
| Configuration  | Manual   | Auto        |
| Web Server     | External | Embedded    |
| Learning Curve | Steeper  | Easier      |
| Speed          | Slower   | Faster      |


🔧 Real Example:
To start a REST API:

Spring:

Set up XML/Java config, create DispatcherServlet, define beans

Spring Boot:

Just add @RestController and run main() – everything else is auto-configured.